 ## Overview
-Analytic-Splatting Forward Shading is a method for computing the color contribution of 3D Gaussians to a pixel by analytically integrating the Gaussian probability density function over the pixel area, rather than sampling the center [S1]. It solves the aliasing artifacts inherent in point-sampling approaches by approximating the pixel area integral using a conditioned logistic function [S1]. It sets itself apart from vanilla 3DGS by providing anti-aliased results and from Mip-Splatting by using a different analytical approximation that maintains higher detail fidelity, albeit with a slight computational overhead [S1].
